## 1. User Stories

> Format: *"As a [role], I want [action] so that [benefit]."*
> All stories traced to functional requirements (Assignment 4) and use cases (Assignment 5).

| Story ID | User Story | Linked FR / UC | Acceptance Criteria | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| US-001 | As a **student**, I want to search for books by title, author, or ISBN so that I can quickly find the resources I need for my studies. | FR-02 / UC02 | Search results returned in ≤ 2 seconds; availability status shown on each result; filters work without page reload. | High |
| US-002 | As a **student**, I want to register and log in using my university email so that my account is linked to my institution. | FR-01 / UC01 | Registration blocked for non-university emails; JWT issued on login; account locked after 5 failed attempts. | High |
| US-003 | As a **student**, I want to borrow or reserve a book online so that I don't have to visit the library in person to secure a resource. | FR-03 / UC03 | Loan record created with 14-day due date; inventory decremented; confirmation email sent within 60 seconds. | High |
| US-004 | As a **student**, I want to view my personal dashboard so that I can see my active loans, due dates, and overdue notices in one place. | FR-04 / UC04 | Dashboard loads within 2 seconds; items due within 3 days highlighted in red; borrowing history shows last 12 months. | High |
| US-005 | As a **student**, I want to receive personalized book recommendations so that I can discover resources relevant to my course without manually searching. | FR-05 / UC05 | Minimum 10 recommendations shown; updated every 24 hours; new students receive course-based defaults within 1 hour. | Medium |
| US-006 | As a **librarian**, I want to add, edit, and delete resources from the catalogue so that the library inventory stays accurate and up to date. | FR-06 / UC06 | New resources indexed in Elasticsearch within 30 seconds; ISBN validated; deletion blocked if active loans exist. | High |
| US-007 | As a **student**, I want to receive automated email reminders before my book is due so that I can return it on time and avoid fines. | FR-07 / UC07 | Emails sent 3 days before, on, and 1 day after due date; email includes title, due date, and dashboard link. | High |
| US-008 | As a **university administrator**, I want to generate and export usage reports so that I can make data-driven decisions about resource procurement. | FR-08 / UC08 | Reports filterable by date, department, and resource type; PDF/CSV export generated within 10 seconds. | Medium |
| US-009 | As an **external developer**, I want to access a versioned REST API with OpenAPI documentation so that I can integrate library features into the university portal. | FR-09 / UC09 | Swagger UI at `/api/v1/docs`; all endpoints return correct HTTP status codes; API sandbox available 24/7. | Medium |
| US-010 | As an **IT administrator**, I want role-based access control enforced so that students, librarians, and admins can only access features relevant to their role. | FR-10 / UC10 | Students cannot access admin endpoints; unauthorized requests return HTTP 403; role changes are audit-logged. | High |
| US-011 | As a **student**, I want to save resources to a personal reading list so that I can keep track of books I want to read in the future. | FR-11 / UC11 | Resource saved in 1 click; up to 10 collections supported; reading list persists across devices and sessions. | Low |
| US-012 | As a **student with a disability**, I want the interface to be fully keyboard-navigable and screen-reader compatible so that I can use the library system independently. | FR-12 / UC02, UC04 | Lighthouse accessibility score ≥ 95; all interactive elements reachable by keyboard; ARIA live regions announced. | High |
| US-013 | As a **system administrator**, I want all student data encrypted with AES-256 and transmitted over TLS so that security and POPIA compliance are maintained. | NFR-09 | Zero plaintext personal data in DB; SSL Labs Grade A; TLS enforced on all endpoints. | High |
| US-014 | As a **librarian**, I want to bulk import resources from a CSV file so that I can add large acquisitions quickly without manual data entry. | FR-06 / UC06a | CSV of up to 1,000 rows processed; invalid rows flagged in error report; valid records indexed within 60 seconds. | Medium |

