## 2. Product Backlog

> Prioritized using MoSCoW. Effort estimated using Fibonacci story points (1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13).

| Story ID | User Story (Summary) | MoSCoW | Story Points | Dependencies | Justification |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| US-002 | Student registration and login | Must-have | 3 | None | All other features require authentication; foundational to the entire system. |
| US-010 | Role-based access control | Must-have | 3 | US-002 | Security baseline; without RBAC, no safe multi-role access is possible. |
| US-013 | AES-256 encryption + TLS | Must-have | 2 | US-002 | POPIA compliance is legally required before any personal data is processed. |
| US-001 | Search library catalogue | Must-have | 5 | US-002 | Core value proposition of SALAS; directly addresses the #1 student pain point. |
| US-003 | Borrow / reserve a book | Must-have | 5 | US-001, US-002 | Key student workflow; required for the system to replace manual library processes. |
| US-004 | Student personal dashboard | Must-have | 5 | US-002, US-003 | Students need a unified view of loans and due dates; critical for engagement. |
| US-006 | Librarian catalogue management | Must-have | 5 | US-010 | Librarians must be able to manage inventory; system has no data without this. |
| US-007 | Automated overdue notifications | Must-have | 3 | US-003 | Directly reduces overdue rates; key success metric for librarian stakeholder. |
| US-012 | Accessible interface (WCAG 2.1 AA) | Must-have | 3 | US-001, US-004 | Legal and ethical obligation; addresses accessibility stakeholder concerns. |
| US-005 | Personalized recommendations | Should-have | 8 | US-001, US-003 | High student value but depends on sufficient borrowing history data. |
| US-008 | Usage reports and analytics | Should-have | 5 | US-003, US-006 | Valuable for admin decisions but not required for core system operation. |
| US-009 | REST API for external integration | Should-have | 5 | US-002, US-001 | Needed for university portal integration but not required for MVP launch. |
| US-014 | Bulk CSV import for librarians | Should-have | 3 | US-006 | Speeds up large acquisitions; not critical until catalogue grows significantly. |
| US-011 | Student reading list | Could-have | 2 | US-001, US-002 | Nice-to-have feature; low effort but low critical impact on core workflows. |

### Prioritization Justification

**Must-have stories** form the MVP: authentication, RBAC, encryption, search, borrowing, dashboard, catalogue management, notifications, and accessibility. These directly map to the highest-priority stakeholder success metrics identified in `STAKEHOLDERS.md` — students finding resources efficiently, librarians managing inventory accurately, and IT administrators maintaining security. Without these, SALAS cannot function as a library system.

**Should-have stories** (recommendations, reporting, API, bulk import) deliver significant value but can be deferred to Sprint 2 and 3 without blocking the MVP. They align with medium-priority stakeholder concerns.

**Could-have stories** (reading list) are low-effort enhancements that improve the student experience but are not required for the system to meet its core purpose.

